It seems a little silly to me to be so fanatical about portability that
Nethack must work on every conceivable terminal.  Face it; anyone who is
still using ADM3As probably doesn't the budget to spare disk space for
large games.

Most terminals *do* have highlighting, at the very least.  Many have
a line-drawing character set.  Why not continue the evolution of the
configuration file to have a user defineable string for every important
feature (this was in 2.3 for MS-DOS machines, but for single chars only):

Some PC type 1 user system:                  A generic Unix system:
OPENDOOR=0x1b "g1" 0x1b "f"                  OPENDOOR={smso} "+" {rmso}
CLOSEDOOR=....                               CLOSEDOOR=....
FLOOR=
VWALL=
HWALL=
ULCORNER=
URCORNER=
LLCORNER=
LRCORNER=
HALL=
WEB=

Then, there could also be 'attribute' strings for monster qualities (tame,
big, small, whatever) of the form
STARTTAME=
STOPTAME=
...

In about 2 months, after a relatively debugged 3.0 is readily available,
and I find some time I will probably implement this myself, if nobody else
does.  I'll submit it to the powers that be for consideration as a permanant
addition.

Any comments?

